{"id": "y0487", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A, an airplane. Air planes are unlikely to get bugs on their wind shields because they fly at high altitudes where bug s cannot reach them. When in motion, the plane moves so quickly through the air that any insects below it are unable to catch up and hit the windshield.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0495", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The man got a pail to catch the draining motor oil, so he was likely doing this in his garage.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0503", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The pencil sharpener was broken in the classroom. Where did the teacher recommend the student go? Well, if it's broken in the classroom, it makes sense that the teacher would suggest going to a place where you can get a new one or fix it. A stationery store is the most logical choice because they sell sharpeners and other supplies. So I think the answer is C, station ery store.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0511", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The string began at C, his hand. Since James trace d the string back to its origin and found it, he must have been holding the other end of the kite string himself. So the string started with his hand when he was flying the kite.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0519", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If you wanted to have fun with a few people, the best choice would be D: friends' house. Being at a friend's house allows for direct interaction, shared activities, and the opportunity to enjoy each other's company in a relaxed environment. While watching TV or going to the cinema can be fun, they are more passive experiences. The fairground s might be exciting but tend to attract larger crowds. A friend' s house offers the most personal and intimate setting for quality time together.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0527", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I'd say it was probably B, playing marbles.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0535", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A snow flake forms in a cloud.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0543", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A beaver is known for building pro wess, their supplies come from wooded area. The correct answer is C, wooded area. Beavers are semi-aquatic rodents that build di kes or dams to create ponds where they can live and raise young. They use branches, bark, leaves, mud, and other materials found in forested areas near bodies of water to construct these structures. So while they need a body of water, the actual building materials come from wooded areas.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 26, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0551", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A, blood moves in a body. Fl ow is the movement of fluids through a system, similar to how blood circ ulates throughout the human body. While leaves move with the wind or water flows in a system, these examples are not directly comparable to the biological process described.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0559", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "As a drought gets worse, the level at an aquifer will decrease. So the correct answer is C. When there's less rain and less water coming into the ground, the underground water supply goes down over time.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
