{"id": "y0855", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's figure this out. So originally, Ed had two more marbles than Doug. Then, after Doug lost some marble s at the playground, Ed ended up with 19 more marbles than him. If we think about it, the difference between how many more marbles Ed had initially and now is exactly how many Doug lost. Since the gap increased by 19, Doug must have lost 19 marbles. That makes sense, right?", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
