{"id": "y1079", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Hunger and eating are primarily regulated by the hypoth alamus. This brain region plays a key role in controlling appetite, satiety, and metabolic processes related to food intake. While other structures like the medulla oblong ata and somatosens ory cortex have roles in basic functions and sensory processing, the hypothalam us is central to hunger regulation. So the correct answer is B, hypothal amus.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1087", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 29, "onset_chunk": 28, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct statement is A. The Human Rights Act 199 8 incorporates the European Convention on Human Rights into UK law. It does not allow courts to invalidate primary legislation, though it can declare laws incompatible with rights, and while it allows individuals to bring cases before courts under certain circumstances, it does not automatically apply to everyone without a legal basis. Additionally, it does not incorporate the EU Charter of Fundamental Rights into UK law after Brexit. So, A is true; B is false because it doesn't invalidate primary legislation outright; C is misleading as there are specific conditions for bringing a case; and D is incorrect since the EU Char ter was not incorporated post- Brexit.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 41, "carrier_ended": null}
